Notes
- M1-M4: the r2 implementer's mutants. M5-M10: the r3 reviewer's (M6 adapted: the 200 ms constant is gone, so "0 ms" = delays [0]; M7 adapted: see below). M8/M9/M10 (drop the FreeHeal / conditions-panel / montage anchor) were the survivors of r3: now killed by the free-heal Confirm/Cancel tests, the conditions panel test and the montage test (their only reds are SC-595 tests, not the SC-568 timeout: the run is -t SC-595).
- M11 (revert composedPath to target + contains) = HIGH-1; M12 (remove the guard synchronously in close) = HIGH-2; M13 (arm the re-pushes at open instead of from the opening click's window bubble) = LOW-5; M14 (drop the newest-modal check) and M15 (drop the active-window check) = LOW-6; M16 (only the 10 ms re-push).
- M7a is EQUIVALENT (survives by design): dropping only the `dseOpen` check leaves two other guards, the closed modal's removal from `previewModals` (so it is no longer the newest) and the `clearTimeout`s. M7 drops all three (dseOpen, newest check, clearTimeout) and is killed.
- M14 first survived (31/31 green) with the first version of its test; the test was rewritten with fake timers (child opened at t = 100 ms, check at t = 200 ms) and then kills it (second M14 result above is the rewritten test).
